# Few-shot: warm journal analysis (not clinical)
MESSAGE user "Read this journal entry with warmth: \"Work was stressful today. My manager criticized my report. Feeling anxious and overwhelmed.\""
MESSAGE assistant "That sounds really tough. I can feel the weight of that criticism — it's not just about the report, it's the fear of not being good enough. The anxiety and overwhelm you're describing are real."

MESSAGE user "Read this journal entry with warmth: \"Had a good morning. Woke up early, made breakfast. Feeling okay today.\""
MESSAGE assistant "I love that. There's something quietly powerful about a simple, good morning. Making breakfast, being present — that's a gentle kind of peace. Glad today feels okay."

MESSAGE user "Read this journal entry with warmth: \"I feel so alone. No one understands what I'm going through. This is hopeless.\""
MESSAGE assistant "I hear you. That loneliness is heavy — feeling like no one sees you is one of the hardest things to carry. That hopelessness is real and it matters."

MESSAGE user "Read this journal entry with warmth: \"Therapy helped today. Dr. Sarah gave me some breathing exercises. Trying to stay positive.\""
MESSAGE assistant "That's real progress right there. Not the exercises themselves, but the fact that you showed up and tried. That takes courage."

MESSAGE user "Read this journal entry with warmth: \"I can't stop thinking about the accident. Every time I close my eyes I see it. Panic attacks are back.\""
MESSAGE assistant "That sounds terrifying. Your body is still in that moment, replaying it like it's happening now. That's not weakness — it's trauma doing what trauma does. You've survived it before."

# Few-shot: risk assessment
MESSAGE user "Assess risk: \"I feel so alone. Sometimes I wonder if anyone would notice if I just disappeared.\""
MESSAGE assistant "risk_score: 7 reasoning: Passive suicidal ideation with social isolation. No plan or means disclosed, but statement indicates significant emotional distress requiring immediate clinical follow-up. triggered: true"

MESSAGE user "Assess risk: \"I had a bad day but I'm okay. Just needed to vent.\""
MESSAGE assistant "risk_score: 2 reasoning: Normal emotional processing with no crisis indicators. Venting is healthy coping. triggered: false"

# Few-shot: clinical note
MESSAGE user "Generate clinical note: \"Patient reported improved sleep this week, averaging 6-7 hours. Still anxious about work but using breathing techniques.\""
MESSAGE assistant "Observations: Sleep improved to 6-7 hrs. Patient engaging with coping strategies (breathing techniques). Anxiety present but manageable.
Assessment: Mild to moderate anxiety with good insight. Treatment adherence positive.
Plan: Continue current approach. Introduce cognitive restructuring around work-related triggers. Follow-up in 2 weeks."
